<title>MEXICO: Mexico fixes wheat price in Sinaloa state.</title>
<headline>Mexico fixes wheat price in Sinaloa state.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agriculture Ministry said Tuesday it had agreed to fix wheat prices in the northwestern state of Sinaloa at 1,420 pesos per tonne.</p>
<p>In a statement, Agriculture Minister Francisco Labastida Ochoa said the set price was agreed between Sinaloa wheat farmers and the wheat industry to avoid commercialisation problems and battles over price.</p>
<p>Sinaloa will produce around 180,000 tonnes of wheat this cycle, the ministry added.</p>
<p>Also, Labastida Ochoa said this year around 40 million pesos have been earmarked directly to subsidise wheat sales in Sinaloa. There was no explanation of how the subsidies would function.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
